@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### Kari's EV charger quote: Ola creates a draft from the van
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "EV charger installation",
  "customer": { "name": "Kari Nordmann", "email": "kari@example.com", "siteAddress": "Fjellveien 12, 5019 Bergen" },
  "lines": [
    { "type": "Labour",   "description": "Installation, electrician", "quantity": 5,  "unit": "h",   "unitPrice": 950,  "vatRate": 0.25 },
    { "type": "Material", "description": "EV charger 11 kW",          "quantity": 1,  "unit": "pcs", "unitPrice": 8990, "vatRate": 0.25 },
    { "type": "Material", "description": "Cable 5x6 mm²",             "quantity": 15, "unit": "m",   "unitPrice": 89,   "vatRate": 0.25 },
    { "type": "Other",    "description": "Call-out / travel",         "quantity": 1,  "unit": "pcs", "unitPrice": 690,  "vatRate": 0.25 }
  ]
}

### Get it back: the ETag header carries the version used for If-Match
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes/{{create.response.body.$.id}}

### List: newest first, filter and search
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes?status=Draft&search=kari&page=1&pageSize=20

### Validation error: missing customer, line without vatRate, too many decimals (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Broken",
  "lines": [ { "type": "Labour", "description": "Work", "quantity": 1.0001, "unit": "h", "unitPrice": 100 } ]
}

### Ola adds the forgotten RCD: full replace of the draft, If-Match = the version he saw (1 → 2)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "EV charger installation",
  "customer": { "name": "Kari Nordmann", "email": "kari@example.com", "siteAddress": "Fjellveien 12, 5019 Bergen" },
  "validUntil": "2026-11-13",
  "lines": [
    { "type": "Labour",   "description": "Installation, electrician", "quantity": 5,  "unit": "h",   "unitPrice": 950,  "vatRate": 0.25 },
    { "type": "Material", "description": "EV charger 11 kW",          "quantity": 1,  "unit": "pcs", "unitPrice": 8990, "vatRate": 0.25 },
    { "type": "Material", "description": "Cable 5x6 mm²",             "quantity": 15, "unit": "m",   "unitPrice": 89,   "vatRate": 0.25 },
    { "type": "Material", "description": "RCD Type B 40A",            "quantity": 1,  "unit": "pcs", "unitPrice": 2450, "vatRate": 0.25 },
    { "type": "Other",    "description": "Call-out / travel",         "quantity": 1,  "unit": "pcs", "unitPrice": 690,  "vatRate": 0.25 }
  ]
}

### The office manager saves with the same stale version: 412, nothing is overwritten
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "EV charger installation",
  "customer": { "name": "Kari Nordmann", "email": "kari@example.com" },
  "validUntil": "2026-11-13",
  "lines": []
}

### Ola sends the version he reviewed (2 → 3); the quote is now locked
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/send
If-Match: "2"

### Editing after send: 409 quote.not_editable (even with a stale tag)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Too late",
  "customer": { "name": "Kari Nordmann", "email": "kari@example.com" },
  "validUntil": "2026-11-13",
  "lines": []
}

### Kari accepts (3 → 4)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/accept
If-Match: "3"

### (Alternative ending) Kari rejects with a reason; the body is optional
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/quotes/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/reject
# If-Match: "3"
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "reason": "Too expensive" }
